## WP-10 Increment U — whole-plane (`shape == null`) free space expansion rooms (2026-10-07)

### Code
- `ExpansionRoom.h/.cpp`: internal `WholePlaneShapeTag` ctor set (shape `IntBox::EMPTY`,
  completion via `IntBox::get_contained_box` → board box, `is_whole_plane()`); public resize
  arm folds a room grown to the board box back into a whole-plane room. `AutorouteEngine.h`
  now only forward-declares `ExpansionRoom`.
- `AutorouteEngine.cpp/.h`: `complete_expansion_room` `WholePlaneShapeTag` overload; the real
  overload rewrites the whole-plane null-shape case to `CompleteShapeInput.shape_type == NULL`
  with `IntBox::get_contained_box` (Java `completeShapeUnlocked` null-start path + the
  `divide_large_room` 4-section split).
- `MazeSearchAlgo.cpp`: maze-start rooms go through the whole-plane overload.
- `ExpansionDrill.cpp`: `calculate_expansion_rooms` uses the whole-plane drill room; interim
  identical-mixture containment guard removed.
- `MazeSearchAlgo.h`: public `set_autoroute_engine()` (used by the drill-expansion test; also
  wired in `get_instance`). The first attempt landed in the private accessor block and the
  test failed to compile — moved next to `set_control()`.

### Java-parity consequence
Drills on obstacle-free boards now DROP (`DrillPage.getDrills` keeps a drill only when each
layer ends with exactly one complete free space room; the whole-board completion yields 4
sections). 10 previously-green empty-board drill tests were reworked to restrained boards
( net-2 `FakeObstacle` walls), not faked back to green.

### Lessons
1. `ShapeTree::insert` transfers leaf `unique_ptr`s to the object's
   `set_search_tree_entries()`; a fake that drops them leaves dangling leaves in `MinAreaTree`
   → SIGSEGV in `MinAreaTree::overlaps`. `FakeObstacle` stores them in a member.
2. `check_layer_with_any_matching_via` bails `NOT_DRILLABLE` when `search_->autoroute_engine()`
   is null — the via-expansion test must set the engine.
3. Wall geometry: `IntBox(4000,0,6000,10000)` → contained rooms `(0,0,4000,10000)` /
   `(6000,0,10000,10000)`; sandwich walls y∈[0,470] + y∈[530,10000], drill (500,500) → thin
   room `(0,470,10000,530)` min_width 60.
4. Stale-binary trap: a build piped through `grep -E " error"` can hide a compile failure and
   rerun the old instrumented test binary.

### Tests (new / reworked)
- `CompleteFreeSpaceExpansionRoom_test.cpp`: +2 (`WholePlaneRoomCompletesToRestrainedFreeSpace`,
  `WholePlaneRoomNeverCompletesToOneRoomOnObstacleFreeTree`); temporary probes removed.
- `DrillPage_test.cpp`: FakeObstacle + walls in the 4 formerly-failing tests → 5/5.
- `DrillPageArray_test.cpp`: FakeObstacle + walls; needs
  `#include "autoroute/ExpansionRoom.h"` for the complete type → 4/4.
- `MazeExpansionEngine_test.cpp`: FakeObstacle + `insert_restraining_walls`; reworked
