## Objective
- Continue the Java → C++ migration of freerouting by implementing the next concrete increment from the recorded roadmap; this iteration ports the Java board-facade API `RoutingBoard.autoroute(Item, RouterSettings, int viaCosts, Stoppable, TimeLimit)` as `RoutingBoard::autoroute(...)` (Increment V), including the `RouterSettings`/`AutorouteControl` prerequisites, tests, and tracking-doc updates.
- Final iteration verdict must be exactly `MIGRATION_CONTINUE` or `MIGRATION_COMPLETE` once ALL work (including doc updates) is verified.

## Important Details
- Baseline before this increment: build green, `ctest --test-dir build` = 755/755.
- Java source of truth: `java/app/freerouting/board/facade/RoutingBoard.java:923-983` (`autoroute` facade). Semantics preserved exactly: `!(item instanceof Connectable) || netCount==0` → `NO_CONNECTIONS`; `netCount>1` → `FRLogger.warn("... netCount > 1 not yet implemented")`; `ctrlSettings.removeUnconnectedVias = false`; plane net + any `ConductionArea` in start set → `CONNECTED_TO_PLANE`; empty `getUnconnectedSet(netNo)` → `ALREADY_CONNECTED`; then `initAutoroute(netNo, ctrl.traceClearanceClassIndex, ..., false)` + `autorouteConnection(...)`; on `ROUTED` → `optChangedArea([netNo], null, tracePullTightAccuracy, ctrl.traceCosts, stoppable, 1000ms)`.
- C++ `Connectable` is a dead draft, so the guard is reproduced with `is_trace() || is_via() || is_pin() || dynamic_cast<const ConductionArea*>` (precedent: `ExpansionRoom.cpp:212-222`).
- `RoutingBoard::fanout` precedent: Java board-facade methods needing autoroute types are declared in `src/board/RoutingBoard.h` and implemented in `src/autoroute/` because the board module cannot reference the autoroute module.
- Java `AutorouteControl` ctors (AutorouteControl.java:117-131): 3-arg = private `(board, settings, settings.getTraceCosts())` + `initNet(netNo, board, settings.getViaCosts())`; 5-arg = private ctor + `initNet(netNo, board, viaCosts)`.
- Java `RouterSettings.getViaCosts()` returns 1 when unset; C++ `RouterScoringSettings::via_costs` is a plain int defaulting to 50 — documented in the new code as the null stand-in (divergence knowingly preserved; do not "fix" the scoring struct default in this increment).
- Java `getTraceCosts()` (RouterSettings.java:949-961) returns empty array if scoring arrays absent, else per-layer `ExpansionCostFactor(horizontal, vertical)`; horizontal/vertical select preferred-direction or against-preferred-direction cost by `getPreferredDirectionIsHorizontal(layer)`; out-of-range layer → 0 (with warn), missing array/too short → 1.0.
- `run_tests` binary location is `build/tests/data/run_tests` (NOT `build/tests/run_tests` — that path does not exist).
- Clock-skew warnings during build are harmless.
- Earlier-iteration latent bug still open (do NOT fix now): `TileShape::cutout` Simplex-hole inversion, `src/geometry/planar/TileShape.cpp` ~line 794.
- Overall migration is not complete; remaining roadmap candidates (from `SOURCE_OF_TRUTH/05_WORK_PACKAGES.md` "Next" bullet ~line 283): (1) `fallbackToBoardVias` fanout via-rule combination (needs `RouterSettings::FanoutSettings` + `BoardRules::via_rules`); (2) `ShapeSearchTree` drill-hole obstacle + clearance feature (Java Via/Pin/Component hole insertion); (3) `TileShape::cutout` Simplex-hole inversion bug; (4) `PullTight*` quality paths.

