 tests and must not be 'fixed': `LineSegment(Polyline,int)` needs >= 3 lines (2-line polylines degenerate to (0,0)-(1,0)), `border_line()` returns *unit* lines, the substitute piece is off-board during the segment recursion, `shove_vias` returns true when it gives up so `insert` fails via the non-empty `shove_via_list` (the claim that a *crossing* foreign trace always fails was a consequence of the abbreviated `ShapeTraceEntries::resort()` and is **wrong** — see WP-10 Inc Q); only divergence: no `reuseEntriesAfterCutout` entry recycling; 17 new gtests; **690/690 ctest** + run_tests green; **WP-10 Inc P done** 2026-10-03: `FoundConnectionInserter` ported (`get_instance`, `insert_trace`, neckdown + micro-neckdown, `insert_via`, fanout diagnostics, both `connect_to_trace` calls) replacing the deleted `InsertFoundConnectionAlgo` stub, together with the `RoutingBoard` forced-trace API (`check_forced_trace_polyline`, `insert_forced_trace_polyline`, `insert_forced_trace_segment`, `connect_to_trace`, `clear_shove_failing_obstacle`), the nullable `ShoveTraceAlgo::spring_over_obstacles` contact pins, `ForcedViaAlgo::check`'s start-trace-circle test, `DrillItem::is_on_layer` and `BasicBoard::mutable_rules`; it also fixed a latent geometry divergence — `Polyline::Polyline(const IntPoint&, const IntPoint&)` built one line instead of Java's three (segment + two 45-degree stubs), which silently turned every single-segment forced insert into a no-op; 17 new gtests; **707/707 ctest** + run_tests green; **WP-10 Inc Q multi-segment insertion + parity fixes done** 2026-10-04: multi-segment (3+ corner) forced-trace insertion now works end to end. Compared against the real Java baseline (the whole `java/app/freerouting` tree compiles with `javac` against the prebuilt 2.1.0 jar, so `TraceShover.insert()`/`ShapeTraceEntries.nextSubstituteTracePiece()` are drivable from a small harness; `board.changedArea` must be set or the trailing `normalize()` NPEs into the log and returns nothing): (1) `ShapeTraceEntries::resort()` is now the full Java port (ShapeTraceEntries.java:462-573) — the old approximation had an early `return` for lists shorter than two entries, so a sole own-net entry survived and made `calculate_stack_levels()` fail; (2) `CalcFromSide::border_intersection` is `std::optional<FloatPoint>` (Java `ShapeEntrySide.borderIntersection` is nullable and `resort()` branches on it — `(0,0)` was the wrong sentinel); (3) `PolylineTrace::combine()` loops like Java instead of recursing, and `own_corner()` returns an owned copy because `combine_at_start()`/`combine_at_end()` kept a `const Point&` into the `corner_points_` cache that `clear_derived_data()` empties (use-after-free); (4) `ClearanceMatrix::get_value(..., /*safety_check=*/true)` subtracted `clearance_safety_margin` where Java adds it, and `RoutingBoard::clearance_value()` skipped the margin, so every shove offset was 16 too small. A crossing foreign trace is now shoved **around** the new shape (Java: `insert` → `true`, one net 2 trace, corners `4000,2000 / 4000,3923 / 7077,3923 / 7077,6077 / 4000,6077 / 4000,8000`); 1 new gtest, 2 re-pinned to Java numbers; **708/708 ctest** + run_tests green; headless blocker closed in WP-10 Inc R: the `AutorouteControl::fanout_start_pin_name` wiring (it also gates `MazeFanoutDiagnostics::enabled()`, which is now compiled, instantiated by `MazeSearchAlgo` and fully wired) **WP-10 Inc R fanout pass done** 2026-10-05: `RoutingBoard::fanout()` is declared in `board/RoutingBoard.h` and defined in the **autoroute** module (`src/autoroute/RoutingBoardFanout.cpp` — the board module may not reference `AutorouteControl`/`AutorouteEngine`; the header forward-declares `autoroute::AutorouteAttemptResult`), plus the board prerequisites `Item::net_count()`/`get_net_no(int)`/`get_connected_set(int)`/`get_unconnected_set(int)`, `Communication::get_resolution(Unit)`, `Pin::relative_location()`/`name()`/`get_center()` (lazy, cached in the new `DrillItem::center_is_set_`) and